.TH CSTR_RFIND 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_rfind \- find the last occurrence of a substring
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_rfind(s, needle);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro just forwards its arguments to cstring_rfind(). The search
starts from the end of the string and takes time linear in the length of
the string plus the length of needle; cstring_rfind(3) has the details.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        cstr to search
needle   Substring to find
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The zero-based index of the last occurrence, or ccol_invalid_size when
the needle is not found
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_rfind (3),
.BR cstr_find (3)
